course: dictionary
lesson: 15545
title: Looks can fool you
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how deep something goes. Superficially means only on the surface, or at first look, not deeply. Think of a thin layer of paint: it covers the top, but the wood underneath may be different.
explain: «The two birds look superficially alike.» At first glance they seem the same, but a closer look may show they are different. The clue is the word alike: the writer means the outside looks similar, and nothing more is said about the inside. Ask yourself: is the writer talking only about the top layer?
explain: Superficially has a second meaning too. «Sam did his sums superficially, guessing most answers.» Here it means quickly and carelessly, without real thought. Check the clues: guessing, no care. Always swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Superficially means only on the surface, or at first look, not deeply.
fact: Superficially is an adverb. The adjective is superficial, as in «a superficial cut».
fact: Superficially can also mean done quickly and carelessly, without real thought or care.
fact: «Superficially similar» is used when two things look alike but are really different, like a whale and a fish.
fact: A good check is to swap in «only on the surface» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The two twins look superficially alike, but they like very different music.» What does superficially mean here? | Very deeply, so they are exactly the same | *Only on the surface, at first look | Loudly, so everyone can hear | Angrily and fast
exercise: «Sam did his maths superficially, guessing most of the answers.» What does superficially mean here? | *Quickly and carelessly, without real thought | Carefully, checking every step | Happily, with a big smile | Slowly, reading each line twice
exercise: «The nurse said the cut was only superficial, so no stitches were needed.» What does superficial mean? | Bright and shiny | *Shallow, hurt only on the skin | Long and thin | Very deep and serious
test: «The two paintings look superficially the same, but one is a copy.» What does superficially suggest? | Painted in the dark | Exactly the same in every detail | Sold for a lot of money | *Only at first look, not when you look deeply
test: «Ella skimmed the book superficially and missed the main idea.» What does superficially mean here? | *Quickly, without real care or depth | Slowly and with great care | Using a magnifying glass | Out loud to the whole class
exam: Which sentence uses superficially to mean only on the surface? | «The dog barked at the postman.» | «Mum bought bread and milk.» | «The walk was long and very hot.» | *«The two cups look superficially alike, but one is cracked inside.»
